pull request: https://github.com/OpenEnergyPlatform/ontology/pull/1728</oeo:OEO_00020426>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://openenergyplatform.org/ontology/oeo/OEO_00020372 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://openenergyplatform.org/ontology/oeo/OEO_00020372">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://openenergyplatform.org/ontology/oeo/OEO_00020366"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000136"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom>
                    <owl:Class>
                        <owl:intersectionOf rdf:parseType="Collection">
                            <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://openenergyplatform.org/ontology/oeo/OEO_00020371"/>
                            <owl:Restriction>
                                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0000056"/>
                                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="https://openenergyplatform.org/ontology/oeo/OEO_00320064"/>
                            </owl:Restriction>
                        </owl:intersectionOf>
                    </owl:Class>
                </owl:someValuesFrom>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>An potential energy storage technology is an energy storage technology that describes how to combine potential energy storage objects and potential energy in charging and decharging processes.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>This technology was introduce for the sake of completeness, but there is no actual use case seen at the moment.</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">potential energy storage technology</rdfs:label>
        <oeo:OEO_00020426>issue: https://github.com/OpenEnergyPlatform/ontology/issues/1572
pull request: https://github.com/OpenEnergyPlatform/ontology/pull/1728</oeo:OEO_00020426>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://openenergyplatform.org/ontology/oeo/OEO_00020407 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://openenergyplatform.org/ontology/oeo/OEO_00020407">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://openenergyplatform.org/ontology/oeo/OEO_00000407"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000136"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom>
                    <owl:Class>
                        <owl:intersectionOf rdf:parseType="Collection">
                            <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://openenergyplatform.org/ontology/oeo/OEO_00000061"/>
                            <owl:Restriction>
                                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0000056"/>
                                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="https://openenergyplatform.org/ontology/oeo/OEO_00020408"/>
                            </owl:Restriction>
                        </owl:intersectionOf>
                    </owl:Class>
                </owl:someValuesFrom>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A sector coupling technology is a technology that intends to connect processes from the electricity, heat, mobility or industrial sectors, as well as their infrastructures.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000600>The aim of sector coupling is usually an optimisation of an energy system (e.g. with respect to cost, environmental impact, sustainability and decarbonisation) by establishing energy flows across sectorial borders</obo:IAO_0000600>
        <rdfs:label>sector coupling technology</rdfs:label>
        <oeo:OEO_00020426>issue: https://github.com/OpenEnergyPlatform/ontology/issues/1521
pull request: https://github.com/OpenEnergyPlatform/ontology/pull/1842</oeo:OEO_00020426>
    </owl:Class>
    


